D_LOGGER_NAMES = (\"rebar\",) (the reconciler's loggers are under rebar)'","_log_integrity.py:12-14: 'There are two such shared parents, not one ... the reconciler subprocess is imported top-level so its modules log under the sibling rebar.reconciler.* root'","_log_integrity.py:50-53 docstring on SHARED_LOGGER_NAMES names rebar.reconciler as a required second root (bug 9151-907b-471d-4a38)","src/rebar/reconciler/__main__.py:434 calls install_stderr_handler(\"rebar\") — pins root=rebar, NOT rebar.reconciler, so the docstring's claim that main() pins rebar.reconciler to WARNING (line 31) is itself stale","src/rebar/reconciler/__init__.py:3-5: reconciler modules log 'inside the rebar hierarchy', covered by the rebar root's NullHandler — corroborates the plan's premise and the docstring's staleness"],"finding":"Step 3 reduces SHARED_LOGGER_NAMES to ('rebar',) and updates the self-test, but does not correct the _log_integrity.py module docstring, which affirmatively documents rebar.reconciler as a separate shared root that MUST be independently guarded ('covering only rebar leaves every rebar.reconciler.* log assertion unprotected'). The plan's stated premise is actually correct (reconciler modules log under rebar.reconciler.*, which propagates up through `rebar`, and the only propagate/level mutation site — reconciler/__main__.py:434 — targets root=\"rebar\", not rebar.reconciler), but the docstring now contradicts the code and asserts the opposite invariant, risking a reviewer revert or an implementer keeping the second entry because the module's own docs say it is load-bearing.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffd7f9f61e5924e1c","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3; tests/_log_integrity.py docstring (lines 10-14, 50-53)","norm_id":"n217fb0e774253f18","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer reads _log_integrity.py docstring still claiming rebar.reconciler must be guarded and rejects the one